The AI provider and its model
20-the-ai-helper
One provider and one model serve every account. The check box marks the provider in use; none marked means the AI is off. Anthropic, OpenAI, Google and DeepSeek come with their connection details and a default model filled in: you supply the key, and M names another model if you want one. Custom is the fifth choice, where you fill in everything yourself, the model included.
The key is typed into the AI helper's own prompt, which shows nothing. It is kept for the helper only (the operating system user sdai), never passes through SD, and is sent only to the provider's address over https, with the certificate checked.
Selecting a provider means that the text accounts send leaves this machine for that provider. An account can send text only if its ai gate is on (the Accounts box). Nothing is on as delivered: no provider, no key and no account.
Enter selects or deselects the provider. M sets the model (a dash goes back to the default), K the key, X clears the key, C fills in Custom, D removes it, A sets the file of certificate authorities for a private CA, L changes a limit. At the prompt: set.ai.
T opens the standing text: a few lines sent first with every AI request from every account, telling the AI what SD is and where its help is. SD ships a default; edit it and choose Save to send your own, or Shipped default to go back. It is invisible to a person asking the AI and does not change their question. A text that names SD's own code is refused.
